sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Client
  participant API as Auth API
  participant Token as Token Auth
  participant RL as Rate Limit And Cooldown
  participant Redis as Redis Bitmap And Cache
  participant OTP as Redis Change Email OTP State
  participant Mongo as MongoDB
  participant Mail as Mail Queue

  Client->>API: POST /auth/email/change-request
  API->>Token: Authenticate access token and tokenVersion
  API->>RL: Apply auth rate limit and user cooldown
  API->>API: Validate and canonicalize new email
  API->>Mongo: Load current user by authenticated userId
  API->>API: Reject if new email equals current email
  API->>Redis: GET bitmap:users:email:v1:ready

  alt Bitmap not ready
    Note over API,Redis: Cannot trust BIT = 0, use MongoDB pre-check
    API->>Mongo: Find user by new canonical email
    alt New email exists
      API-->>Client: 409 Email already exists
    else New email missing
      API->>OTP: Store old-email and new-email OTP state
      API->>Mail: Send OTP to old email
      API->>Mail: Send OTP to new email
      API-->>Client: OTPs sent
    end
  else Bitmap ready
    API->>Redis: GETBIT bitmap:users:email:v1 at new-email index
  end

  alt Ready and BIT = 0
    Note over API,Redis: New email is treated as available for pre-check
    API->>OTP: Store old-email and new-email OTP state
    API->>Mail: Send OTP to old email
    API->>Mail: Send OTP to new email
    API-->>Client: OTPs sent
  else Ready and BIT = 1
    Note over API,Redis: Maybe exists, must verify through cache or MongoDB
    API->>Redis: GET user:email:{sha256(newEmail)}
    alt Positive cache hit
      API-->>Client: 409 Email already exists
    else Positive cache miss
      API->>Mongo: Find user by new canonical email
      alt New email exists
        API->>Redis: SET user:email:{hash}
        API-->>Client: 409 Email already exists
      else New email missing
        API->>OTP: Store old-email and new-email OTP state
        API->>Mail: Send OTP to old email
        API->>Mail: Send OTP to new email
        API-->>Client: OTPs sent
      end
    end
  end

  Client->>API: POST /auth/email/change-verify
  API->>Token: Authenticate access token and tokenVersion
  API->>OTP: Verify old-email and new-email OTPs
  API->>Mongo: Update email under unique email index

  alt Update succeeds
    API->>Redis: DEL old user:email:{hash}
    API->>Redis: SET new user:email:{hash}
    API->>Redis: SETBIT bitmap:users:email:v1 for new email
    API->>Redis: DEL nf:email:{newEmailHash}
    API-->>Client: Email changed
  else Duplicate key race
    API-->>Client: 409 Email already exists
  end
